      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): sync root --help command descriptions with live command registrations",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #98978: `openclaw --help` rendered root command descriptions from static placeholder catalogs that had drifted from the real registered command descriptions. 29 commands showed different text in `--help` vs `<command> --help` and shell completion. Most critically, `config` hid `patch`/`schema` subcommands from root help discovery.\n\nRoot cause: the placeholder descriptor catalogs (`core-command-descriptors.ts`, `subcli-descriptors.ts`) were copied from live descriptions at one point in time, but the real command modules continued to evolve independently with no contract keeping them in sync.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nPer the repo's one-canonical-path rule, updated the catalogs to match the current live descriptions from registered command modules. Key corrections:\n\n- `config`: added `patch`/`schema` + changed \"Default:\" → \"Run without subcommand for\"\n- `setup`: \"Initialize local config...\" → \"Alias for openclaw onboard\"  \n- `crestodian`: \"interactive setup and repair assistant\" → \"ring-zero setup and repair helper\"\n- `daemon`: \"legacy alias\" → \"launchd/systemd/schtasks\"\n- Plus 25 other description syncs\n\n## User Impact\n\n- `openclaw --help` now shows the same descriptions as `<command> --help` and tab completion\n- `config patch` and `config schema` are now discoverable from root help\n- No behavioral changes — purely metadata/help text alignment\n\n## Evidence\n\n- [x] `pnpm test src/cli/program/help.test.ts` — 6 tests pass\n- [x] `pnpm exec oxlint` passes on changed files\n- [x] Full 29-command diff verified against issue #98978 table\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
